# Where this build reads its data from.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and adjust. `.env.local` is gitignored, so nothing here is
# committed and nothing here is a secret.
#
# This variable is load-bearing and was previously implicit. `next.config.ts` fell
# back to a hardcoded deployment hostname when it was unset, so a fresh clone, a CI
# runner and a hosting build all silently read a backend chosen by a string
# literal rather than by anything the operator stated. Local verification stayed
# green against a backend nobody was looking at: one company page served a price
# two sessions stale from a different deployment while every check passed.
#
# The build now prints which origin it chose, and logs a warning when a production
# build falls back. Set this explicitly for anything you intend to audit.
#
#   local development   http://127.0.0.1:8111     (backend running on this machine)
#   production build    https://<your-backend-host>
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8111
